From: Julian Waller <me@julusian.co.uk>
Date: Sun, 8 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Remove boost_system from find_package COMPONENTS

With CMake 4.x (CMP0167 NEW), FindBoost is removed and BoostConfig.cmake
is used exclusively. In modern Ubuntu/Boost releases, boost_system is
fully header-only and boost_systemConfig.cmake is no longer installed as
a separate package. Removing it from COMPONENTS lets the build proceed;
the boost::system::error_code type is still available via Boost::headers.
---
 src/CMakeModules/Bootstrap_Linux.cmake | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/CMakeModules/Bootstrap_Linux.cmake b/src/CMakeModules/Bootstrap_Linux.cmake
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/src/CMakeModules/Bootstrap_Linux.cmake
+++ b/src/CMakeModules/Bootstrap_Linux.cmake
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@ MARK_AS_ADVANCED (CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX)
 if (USE_STATIC_BOOST)
 	SET (Boost_USE_STATIC_LIBS ON)
 endif()
-find_package(Boost 1.74.0 COMPONENTS system thread filesystem log_setup log locale regex date_time coroutine REQUIRED)
+find_package(Boost 1.74.0 COMPONENTS thread filesystem log_setup log locale regex date_time coroutine REQUIRED)
 find_package(FFmpeg REQUIRED)
 find_package(OpenGL REQUIRED COMPONENTS OpenGL GLX EGL)
 find_package(GLEW REQUIRED)
